  "provenance": {
    "extended_at": "2026-08-23T06:58:55.438891+00:00",
    "extended_by": "energy-sprint/packs/extend_packs.py",
    "notes": "PF units are '%' because SunSpec declares PF as Pct on models 101-103. The converter turns 95 Pct into the 0.95 ratio power_factor is declared to hold.",
    "rationale": "The shipped pack covers 8 canonicals from the inverter's power and DC points but carries nothing for AC current, line voltage, reactive power or power factor \u2014 so a Fronius Primo resolves its output and loses its grid-quality measurements. Adding the remaining aggregate points from SunSpec 101/103.\n\nIt also claimed the aliases `sunspec`, `sma` and `solaredge`. Packs load in filename order and the first claimant of an alias wins, so `oem=solaredge` resolved to the Fronius pack \u2014 whose mappings use bare SunSpec names and share not one tag with SolarEdge's I_/M_ spellings. Every SolarEdge tag missed. Those aliases now belong to their own packs.",
    "registry_field_count": 394,
    "tier": "vendor_doc"
  },
  "source": "SunSpec Alliance Modbus models 101-103 (single/split/three-phase inverter), a public standard. Point names are normative.",
